  "cells": [
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# AnimalEmotion AI – Deep Learning-Based Animal Emotion Recognition System\n","## Phase 1: Rigorous Dataset Audit\n","\n","This notebook performs only a pre-training dataset audit. It does not train a model and does not create train/validation/test splits. Authentication and file outputs are isolated from the source code.\n","\n","**Primary dataset:** `kk2004/animalemotion` on Kaggle: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/kk2004/animalemotion/data\n","\n","All findings must be interpreted from data evidence. Folder names are never treated as confirmed labels unless independent annotation evidence supports that interpretation."]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Audit objectives and constraints\n","- Verify the downloaded archive safely.\n","- Discover, inspect, and inventory all images.\n","- Record corruption, dimensions, channels, transparency, file sizes, and duplicates.\n","- Inspect folder hierarchies and annotation CSV/JSON files.\n","- Separate confirmed labels from inferred folder names.\n","- Measure class imbalance only where a label is supported.\n","- Assess potential data leakage without modifying or deleting source images.\n","- Produce reproducible machine-readable reports and an evidence-based Phase 2 recommendation."]},
    {"cell_type":"code","execution_metadata":{"id":"imports"},"execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# Environment setup and reproducibility\n","from pathlib import Path\n","import os, sys, json, zipfile, hashlib, stat, shutil, random, re, textwrap, traceback\n","import pandas as pd\n","import numpy as np\n","from tqdm.auto import tqdm\n","from PIL import Image, ImageOps, UnidentifiedImageError, ImageFile\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import seaborn as sns\n","\n","import torch\n","import torchvision\n","import cv2\n","import sklearn\n","\n","SEED = 42\n","random.seed(SEED); np.random.seed(SEED); torch.manual_seed(SEED)\n","if torch.cuda.is_available():\n","    torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(SEED)\n","torch.backends.cudnn.deterministic = True\n","torch.backends.cudnn.benchmark = False\n","sns.set_theme(style='whitegrid')\n","\n","ROOT = Path('/content/animalemotion')\n","RAW_DIR = ROOT/'raw'\n","EXTRACT_DIR = ROOT/'dataset'\n","REPORT_DIR = ROOT/'reports'\n","for d in (ROOT, RAW_DIR, EXTRACT_DIR, REPORT_DIR): d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n","\n","print('PyTorch:', torch.__version__)\n","print('torchvision:', torchvision.__version__)\n","print('CUDA available:', torch.cuda.is_available())\n","if torch.cuda.is_available(): print('GPU:', torch.cuda.get_device_name(0))"]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Kaggle authentication\n","Use Colab Secrets (`KAGGLE_USERNAME` and `KAGGLE_KEY`) whenever possible. The fallback asks for a local `kaggle.json` upload. Credentials are written only to `/root/.kaggle`, never to a report or notebook.\n","\n","In Colab: **Secrets** → add `KAGGLE_USERNAME` and `KAGGLE_KEY`, then enable notebook access."]},
    {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# Never hardcode credentials\n","kaggle_dir = Path.home()/'.kaggle'\n","kaggle_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n","kaggle_json = kaggle_dir/'kaggle.json'\n","username = key = None\n","\n","# Colab Secrets\n","try:\n","    from google.colab import userdata\n","    username = userdata.get('KAGGLE_USERNAME')\n","    key = userdata.get('KAGGLE_KEY')\n","except Exception:\n","    pass\n","\n","# Secure upload fallback\n","if not (username and key):\n","    if kaggle_json.exists():\n","        try:\n","            cfg = json.loads(kaggle_json.read_text())\n","            username, key = cfg.get('username'), cfg.get('key')\n","        except Exception as exc:\n","            print('Existing kaggle.json could not be read:', exc)\n","    if not (username and key):\n","        try:\n","            from google.colab import files\n","            print('Upload a Kaggle API token (kaggle.json). No credential values will be printed.')\n","            uploaded = files.upload()\n","            if 'kaggle.json' in uploaded:\n","                kaggle_json.write_bytes(uploaded['kaggle.json'])\n","                cfg = json.loads(kaggle_json.read_text())\n","                username, key = cfg.get('username'), cfg.get('key')\n","        except Exception as exc:\n","            print('Credential setup could not complete:', exc)\n","\n","if username and key:\n","    kaggle_json.write_text(json.dumps({'username': username, 'key': key}))\n","    os.chmod(kaggle_json, stat.S_IRUSR | stat.S_IWUSR)\n","    os.environ['KAGGLE_USERNAME'] = username\n","    os.environ['KAGGLE_KEY'] = key\n","    print('Kaggle authentication configured securely.')\n","else:\n","    raise RuntimeError('No Kaggle credentials found. Configure Colab Secrets or upload kaggle.json.')"]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Kaggle download and protected extraction"]},
    {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# Install Kaggle CLI, download once if needed, then extract safely\n","import subprocess\n","subprocess.run([sys.executable, '-m', 'pip', 'install', '-q', 'kaggle'], check=True)\n","\n","DATASET_SLUG = 'kk2004/animalemotion'\n","archive_files = list(RAW_DIR.glob('*.zip'))\n","if not archive_files:\n","    result = subprocess.run(['kaggle','datasets','download','-d',DATASET_SLUG,'-p',str(RAW_DIR),'--force'], capture_output=True, text=True)\n","    if result.returncode != 0:\n","        raise RuntimeError('Kaggle download failed:\\n'+result.stderr)\n","    print(result.stdout.strip())\n","archive_files = sorted(RAW_DIR.glob('*.zip'))\n","if not archive_files:\n","    raise RuntimeError('Download succeeded without a ZIP archive.')\n","print('Archive(s):', [p.name for p in archive_files])\n","\n","def is_zip_symlink(info):\n","    mode = info.external_attr >> 16\n","    return stat.S_ISLNK(mode)\n","\n","def safe_extract_zip(zip_path: Path, destination: Path):\n","    destination = destination.resolve()\n","    extracted=[]; rejected=[]\n","    with zipfile.ZipFile(zip_path) as zf:\n","        for info in zf.infolist():\n","            if info.filename.startswith('/') or re.match(r'^[A-Za-z]:', info.filename):\n","                rejected.append((info.filename, 'absolute path')); continue\n","            rel = Path(info.filename)\n","            if '..' in rel.parts:\n","                rejected.append((info.filename, 'parent traversal')); continue\n","            if is_zip_symlink(info):\n","                rejected.append((info.filename, 'symbolic link')); continue\n","            target = (destination/rel).resolve()\n","            if destination not in target.parents and target != destination:\n","                rejected.append((info.filename, 'escaped destination')); continue\n","            if info.is_dir():\n","                target.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True); continue\n","            target.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n","            with zf.open(info) as src, open(target, 'wb') as dst:\n","                shutil.copyfileobj(src,dst)
","            extracted.append(str(target.relative_to(destination)))\n","    return extracted, rejected\n","\n","all_extracted=[]; all_rejected=[]\n","for archive in archive_files:
","    ext,rej=safe_extract_zip(archive, EXTRACT_DIR)
","    all_extracted += ext; all_rejected += rej
","print(f'Safely extracted {len(all_extracted)} files; rejected {len(all_rejected)} entries.')\n","(REPORT_DIR/'safe_extraction.json').write_text(json.dumps({'extracted_count':len(all_extracted),'rejected_count':len(all_rejected),'rejected_entries':[{'entry':r[0],'reason':r[1]} for r in all_rejected]},indent=2))"]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. Recursive directory inspection and image discovery"]},
    {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["IMAGE_EXTS={'.jpg','.jpeg','.png','.bmp','.gif','.tif','.tiff','.webp','.jfif','.heic','.heif'}\n","NON_IMAGE_EXTS={'.csv','.json','.txt','.yaml','.yml','.xml','.xls','.xlsx'}\n","all_files=[p for p in EXTRACT_DIR.rglob('*') if p.is_file()]\n","image_files=[p for p in all_files if p.suffix.lower() in IMAGE_EXTS]\n","annotation_files=[p for p in all_files if p.suffix.lower() in {'.csv','.json','.xlsx','.xls','.yaml','.yml','xml'}]\n","print(f'Total files: {len(all_files):,}; image candidates: {len(image_files):,}; annotation candidates: {len(annotation_files):,}')\n","\n","# Folder hierarchy summary\n","folder_counts={}\n","for p in all_files:\n","    rel=p.relative_to(EXTRACT_DIR)\n","    for i in range(1,len(rel.parts)):\n","        folder='/'.join(rel.parts[:i])\n","        folder_counts[folder]=folder_counts.get(folder,0)+1\n","folder_df=pd.DataFrame([{'folder':k,'file_count':v} for k,v in sorted(folder_counts.items())]).sort_values('folder')\n","folder_df.to_csv(REPORT_DIR/'folder_hierarchy.csv',index=False)\n","folder_df.head(30)"]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 5. Image metadata and integrity audit\n","The audit distinguishes file-extension candidates, successfully opened images, and files that are corrupted or unsupported."]},
    {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["ImageFile.LOAD_TRUNCATED_IMAGES=False\n","\n","def sha256_file(path, chunk=1024*1024):\n","    h=hashlib.sha256()\n","    with open(path,'rb') as f:\n","        for b in iter(lambda:f.read(chunk),b''): h.update(b)\n","    return h.hexdigest()\n","\n","rows=[]\n","for p in tqdm(image_files,desc='Auditing images'):\n","    rel=p.relative_to(EXTRACT_DIR).as_posix()\n","    try:\n","        stat_info=p.stat(); file_size=stat_info.st_size\n","        sha=sha256_file(p)\n","        with Image.open(p) as im:\n","            im.verify()\n","        with Image.open(p) as im:\n","            im.load(); fmt=im.format; mode=im.mode\n","            width,height=im.size\n","            exif=dict(im.getexif()) if getattr(im,'getexif',None) else {}\n","            has_alpha='A' in mode or ('transparency' in im.info) or (im.mode=='P' and 'transparency' in im.info)\n","            if mode=='RGB': channels=3\n","            elif mode=='RGBA': channels=4\n","            elif mode=='L': channels=1\n","            elif mode=='LA': channels=2\n","            else: channels=len(im.getbands())\n","            im_gray=ImageOps.grayscale(im)\n","            extrema=im_gray.getextrema()
","            mean=np.asarray(im,dtype=np.uint8).mean() if im.size[0]*im.size[1]>0 else np.nan\n","            rows.append({'relative_path':rel,'filename':p.name,'format':fmt,'mode':mode,'channels':channels,'width':width,'height':height,'aspect_ratio':width/height if height else np.nan,'file_bytes':file_size,'sha256':sha,'alpha_or_transparency':bool(has_alpha),'exif_tag_count':len(exif),'integrity':'ok','error':''})
","    except (UnidentifiedImageError, OSError, SyntaxError, ValueError) as exc:
","        sha=None
","        try:
","            sha=sha256_file(p)
","            file_size=p.stat().st_size
","        except Exception:
","            file_size=None
","        rows.append({'relative_path':rel,'filename':p.name,'format':None,'mode':None,'channels':np.nan,'width':np.nan,'height':np.nan,'aspect_ratio':np.nan,'file_bytes':file_size,'sha256':sha,'alpha_or_transparency':False,'exif_tag_count':0,'integrity':'corrupted_or_unreadable','error':f'{type(exc).__name__}: {str(exc)}'})
","    except Exception as exc:
","        rows.append({'relative_path':rel,'filename':p.name,'format':None,'mode':None,'channels':np.nan,'width':np.nan,'height':np.nan,'aspect_ratio':np.nan,'file_bytes':p.stat().st_size,'sha256':sha256_file(p),'alpha_or_transparency':False,'exif_tag_count':0,'integrity':'audit_exception','error':f'{type(exc).__name__}: {str(exc)}'})
","\n","inventory=pd.DataFrame(rows)
","inventory.to_csv(REPORT_DIR/'image_inventory.csv',index=False)
","corrupt=inventory[inventory['integrity']!='ok'].copy()
","corrupt.to_csv(REPORT_DIR/'corrupted_images.csv',index=False)
","print('Inventory:',len(inventory),'images; readable:',int((inventory.integrity=='ok').sum()),'problems:',len(corrupt))"]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 6. Dimensions, channels, transparency, and file size"]},
    {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["valid=inventory[inventory['integrity']=='ok'].copy()
","summary={}
","if not valid.empty:
","    summary={
","      'readable_image_count':int(len(valid)),
","      'width_min':int(valid.width.min()),'width_median':float(valid.width.median()),'width_max':int(valid.width.max()),
","      'height_min':int(valid.height.min()),'height_median':float(valid.height.median()),'height_max':int(valid.height.max()),
","      'aspect_ratio_median':float(valid.aspect_ratio.median()),
","      'formats':valid.format.value_counts(dropna=False).to_dict(),
","      'modes':valid.mode.value_counts(dropna=False).to_dict(),
","      'transparency_image_count':int(valid.alpha_or_transparency.sum()),
","      'file_bytes_min':int(valid.file_bytes.min()),'file_bytes_median':float(valid.file_bytes.median()),'file_bytes_max':int(valid.file_bytes.max()),
","    }
","print(json.dumps(summary,indent=2))
","(REPORT_DIR/'dimension_summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary,indent=2))
","\n","if not valid.empty:
","    fig,axes=plt.subplots(2,2,figsize=(14,10))
","    axes[0,0].hist(valid.width,bins=40); axes[0,0].set(title='Width Distribution',xlabel='Width (px)',ylabel='Count')
","    axes[0,1].hist(valid.height,bins=40); axes[0,1].set(title='Height Distribution',xlabel='Height (px)',ylabel='Count')
","    sns.scatterplot(data=valid,x='width',y='height',alpha=.45,ax=axes[1,0]); axes[1,0].set(title='Resolution Scatter')
","    axes[1,1].hist(valid.file_bytes/1024,bins=50); axes[1,1].set(title='File Size Distribution',xlabel='KB',ylabel='Count')
","    plt.tight_layout(); plt.savefig(REPORT_DIR/'resolution_and_size_plots.png',dpi=150); plt.show()
"]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 7. Exact duplicate detection (SHA-256)"]},
    {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["hash_counts=valid.groupby('sha256').size().sort_values(ascending=False)
","duplicate_hashes=hash_counts[hash_counts>1]
","exact_dups=valid[valid.sha256.isin(duplicate_hashes.index)].sort_values(['sha256','relative_path']).copy()
","exact_dups.to_csv(REPORT_DIR/'exact_duplicates.csv',index=False)
","exact_duplicate_groups=exact_dups.groupby('sha256').agg(paths=('relative_path',lambda s:'\\n'.join(s)),count=('relative_path','size')).reset_index()
","exact_duplicate_groups.to_csv(REPORT_DIR/'exact_duplicate_groups.csv',index=False)
","print('Exact duplicate groups:',len(exact_duplicate_groups),'files in duplicate groups:',len(exact_dups))"]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 8. Optional perceptual duplicate detection\n","Set `ENABLE_PHASH=True` to run perceptual hashing. It is off by default to avoid unexpectedly long Colab execution."]},
    {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["ENABLE_PHASH=False\n","PHASH_THRESHOLD=6
","phash_rows=[]
","if ENABLE_PHASH:
","    try:
","        subprocess.run([sys.executable,'-m','pip','install','-q','ImageHash'],check=True)
","        import imagehash
","        for _,r in tqdm(valid.iterrows(),total=len(valid),desc='Perceptual hashing'):
","            p=EXTRACT_DIR/r.relative_path
","            try:
","                with Image.open(p) as im:
","                    im=ImageOps.exif_transpose(im).convert('RGB')
","                    phash_rows.append({'relative_path':r.relative_path,'phash':str(imagehash.phash(im,hash_size=16))})
","            except Exception as exc:
","                phash_rows.append({'relative_path':r.relative_path,'phash':None,'error':str(exc)})
","        phash_df=pd.DataFrame(phash_rows)
","        phash_df.to_csv(REPORT_DIR/'perceptual_hashes.csv',index=False)
","        # Conservative pairwise comparison for Hamming distance <= threshold
","        pairs=[]
","        valid_phash=[x for x in phash_rows if x.get('phash')]
","        for i,a in enumerate(valid_phash):
","            ha=imagehash.hex_to_hash(a['phash'])
","            for b in valid_phash[i+1:]:
","                hb=imagehash.hex_to_hash(b['phash'])
","                d=ha-hb
","                if d<=PHASH_THRESHOLD:
","                    pairs.append({'path_a':a['relative_path'],'path_b':b['relative_path'],'hamming_distance':int(d),'threshold':PHASH_THRESHOLD})
","        pd.DataFrame(pairs).to_csv(REPORT_DIR/'perceptual_duplicate_candidates.csv',index=False)
","        print('Perceptual candidate pairs:',len(pairs))
","    except Exception as exc:
","        print('Perceptual hashing unavailable:',exc)
","else:
","    pd.DataFrame(columns=['relative_path','phash']).to_csv(REPORT_DIR/'perceptual_hashes.csv',index=False)
","    print('Perceptual hashing skipped; set ENABLE_PHASH=True to run it.')"]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 9. Annotation and folder hierarchy inspection"]},
    {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["annotation_manifest=[]
","csv_tables={}; json_samples={}
","for p in annotation_files:
","    rel=p.relative_to(EXTRACT_DIR).as_posix()
","    item={'relative_path':rel,'suffix':p.suffix.lower(),'status':'unknown','row_count':None,'columns':[], 'top_level_keys':[],'error':''}
","    try:
","        if p.suffix.lower()=='.csv':
","            df=pd.read_csv(p)
","            item.update(status='readable',row_count=len(df),columns=[str(c) for c in df.columns])
","            csv_tables[rel]=df
","            df.head(100).to_csv(REPORT_DIR/(re.sub(r'[^A-Za-z0-9_.-]','_',p.name)+'.sample.csv'),index=False)
","        elif p.suffix.lower()=='.json':
","            obj=json.loads(p.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
","            item['status']='readable'
","            if isinstance(obj,dict):
","                item['top_level_keys']=list(obj.keys())[:100]
","                json_samples[rel]=obj
","            elif isinstance(obj,list):
","                item['row_count']=len(obj)
","                if obj and isinstance(obj[0],dict): item['top_level_keys']=list(obj[0].keys())[:100]
","                json_samples[rel]=obj
","        elif p.suffix.lower() in {'.xlsx','.xls'}:
","            xl=pd.ExcelFile(p)
","            item.update(status='readable',columns=xl.sheet_names)
","    except Exception as exc:
","        item.update(status='unreadable',error=f'{type(exc).__name__}: {str(exc)}')
","    annotation_manifest.append(item)
","pd.DataFrame(annotation_manifest).to_csv(REPORT_DIR/'annotation_manifest.csv',index=False)
","print('Annotation candidates:',len(annotation_manifest))"]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 10. Evidence-based label discovery\n","This section only marks labels `confirmed` when a CSV column is explicitly identified by name or JSON keys support label mapping. Folder components remain `inferred_folder_name` and are never elevated to confirmed labels."]},
    {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["def norm_name(s):
","    return re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]+','_',str(s).lower()).strip('_')
","emotion_tokens={'emotion','emotions','expression','expressions','sentiment','mood','label'}
","species_tokens={'species','animal','animal_type','animal_class','breed','pet','dog','cat'}
","generic_tokens={'class','category','target'}
","label_evidence=[]
","for rel,df in csv_tables.items():
","    cols=[str(c) for c in df.columns]
","    for c in cols:
","        n=norm_name(c)
","        kind='other'
","        if n in emotion_tokens: kind='confirmed_emotion_column'
","        elif n in species_tokens: kind='confirmed_species_column'
","        elif n in generic_tokens: kind='candidate_label_column_requires_review'
","        if kind!='other':
","            vals=df[c].dropna().astype(str).value_counts()
","            label_evidence.append({'source_type':'CSV','source_path':rel,'column':c,'evidence_type':kind,'unique_count':int(df[c].nunique(dropna=True)),'top_values':vals.head(20).to_dict()})
","pd.DataFrame(label_evidence).to_csv(REPORT_DIR/'confirmed_label_evidence.csv',index=False)
","print('Label evidence rows:',len(label_evidence))
","\n","# Inferred folder names only\n","folder_inference=[]
","for p in image_files:
","    rel=p.relative_to(EXTRACT_DIR)
","    parts=rel.parts[:-1]
","    for depth,part in enumerate(parts,1):
","        folder_inference.append({'relative_image_path':rel.as_posix(),'folder_depth':depth,'inferred_folder_name':part,'status':'inferred_folder_name_only','confirmed_label':False})
","pd.DataFrame(folder_inference).to_csv(REPORT_DIR/'inferred_folder_hierarchy.csv',index=False)
","\n","# Summarize candidate label distributions only when evidence was detected\n","distribution_frames=[]
","for item in label_evidence:
","    df=csv_tables[item['source_path']]
","    counts=df[item['column']].fillna('<missing>').astype(str).value_counts().rename_axis('label').reset_index(name='count')
","    counts['source_path']=item['source_path']; counts['column']=item['column']; counts['evidence_type']=item['evidence_type']
","    distribution_frames.append(counts)
","if distribution_frames:
","    class_dist=pd.concat(distribution_frames,ignore_index=True)
","else:
","    class_dist=pd.DataFrame(columns=['label','count','source_path','column','evidence_type'])
","class_dist.to_csv(REPORT_DIR/'class_distribution.csv',index=False)
","class_dist.head(30)"]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 11. Class distribution and imbalance analysis"]},
    {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["imbalance=[]
","for (source,col),g in class_dist.groupby(['source_path','column'],dropna=False):
","    counts=g['count'].astype(int)
","    if len(counts):
","        total=int(counts.sum()); vmax=int(counts.max()); vmin=int(counts.min())
","        imbalance.append({'source_path':source,'column':col,'class_count':int(len(counts)),'total_labeled_rows':total,'largest_class_count':vmax,'smallest_class_count':vmin,'max_to_min_ratio':float(vmax/vmin if vmin>0 else np.inf),'status':'evidence_based'})
","imbalance_df=pd.DataFrame(imbalance)
","imbalance_df.to_csv(REPORT_DIR/'imbalance_analysis.csv',index=False)
","\n","if not class_dist.empty:
","    sample=class_dist.sort_values('count',ascending=False)
","    plt.figure(figsize=(12,max(5,min(16,len(sample)/2))))
","    sns.barplot(data=sample,x='count',y='label',hue='column',dodge=False)
","    plt.title('Evidence-Based Label Distribution'); plt.tight_layout()
","    plt.savefig(REPORT_DIR/'class_distribution.png',dpi=150,bbox_inches='tight'); plt.show()
","else:
","    print('No confirmed/evidence-based label distribution could be derived. Folder names are retained only as inferred evidence.')"]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 12. Species/emotion hierarchy discovery where supported"]},
    {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["hierarchy_records=[]
","for item in label_evidence:
","    df=csv_tables[item['source_path']]
","    hierarchy_records.append({'source_path':item['source_path'],'column':item['column'],'evidence_type':item['evidence_type'],'hierarchy_supported':True,'filename_mapping_not_checked':True})
","# Add folder hierarchy only as a separate inferred relationship
","for depth in sorted(set(r['folder_depth'] for r in folder_inference)) if folder_inference else []:
","    vals=sorted(set(r['inferred_folder_name'] for r in folder_inference if r['folder_depth']==depth))
","    hierarchy_records.append({'source_path':'folder_structure','column':f'depth_{depth}','evidence_type':'inferred_folder_name_only','hierarchy_supported':False,'inferred_names':vals[:200]})
","pd.DataFrame(hierarchy_records).to_csv(REPORT_DIR/'hierarchy_discovery.csv',index=False)
","print('Hierarchy discovery report written.')"]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 13. Sample and duplicate visualizations"]},
    {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["def mosaic(paths, title, out_path, cols=5, thumb=180):
","    paths=[EXTRACT_DIR/p if isinstance(p,str) else p for p in paths]
","    if not paths:
","        print(title+': no examples available'); return
","    rows=(len(paths)+cols-1)//cols
","    fig,axes=plt.subplots(rows,cols,figsize=(cols*3,rows*3)); axes=np.atleast_1d(axes).ravel()
","    for ax in axes: ax.axis('off')
","    for ax,p in zip(axes,paths):
","        try:
","            im=Image.open(p).convert('RGB')
","            im.thumbnail((thumb,thumb))
","            ax.imshow(im); ax.set_title(p.name[:28],fontsize=8)
","        except Exception:
","            ax.text(.5,.5,'Unreadable',ha='center',va='center')
","    fig.suptitle(title); plt.tight_layout(); plt.savefig(out_path,dpi=150,bbox_inches='tight'); plt.close(fig)
","\n","rng=np.random.default_rng(SEED)
","readable_paths=valid.relative_path.tolist()
","sample_paths=rng.choice(readable_paths,size=min(20,len(readable_paths)),replace=False).tolist() if readable_paths else []
","mosaic(sample_paths,'Random readable image sample',REPORT_DIR/'random_sample_mosaic.png')
","mosaic(exact_dups.relative_path.drop_duplicates().head(20).tolist(),'Exact duplicate examples',REPORT_DIR/'exact_duplicate_examples.png')
","mosaic(corrupt.relative_path.head(20).tolist(),'Corrupted/unreadable candidates',REPORT_DIR/'corrupt_examples.png')"]},
    {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 14. Suspicious-label and filename review"]},
    {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["suspicious=[]
","# Rare or missing evidence-based labels
","for _,r in class_dist[class_dist['count']<5].iterrows():
","    suspicious.append({'issue':'rare_label','source_path':r['source_path'],'column':r['column'],'evidence':r['evidence_type'],'value':r['label'],'count':int(r['count'])})
","# Duplicate stems across folders may indicate inconsistent naming or near-leakage
","stem_locations=valid.assign(stem=valid.filename.map(lambda x:Path(x).stem)).groupby('stem').agg(locations=('relative_path',lambda s:'; '.join(sorted(s))),count=('relative_path','size')).reset_index()
","stem_conflicts=stem_locations[stem_locations['count']>1]
","for _,r in stem_conflicts.head(500).iterrows():
","    suspicious.append({'issue':'duplicate_filename_stem_across_inventory','value':r['stem'],'count':int(r['count']),'locations':r['locations']})
","# Unusual aspect ratios and suspiciously tiny/large resolutions
","if not valid.empty:
","    for _,r in valid[(valid.width<32)|(valid.height<32)|(valid.aspect_ratio<.25)|(valid.aspect_ratio>4)].iterrows():
","        suspicious.append({'issue':'unusual_resolution_or_aspect_ratio','value':r.relative_path,'count':1,'width':r.width,'height':r.height,'aspect_ratio':r.aspect_ratio})
","pd.DataFrame(suspicious).to_csv(REPORT_DIR/'suspicious_label_review.csv',index=False)
","print('Suspicious review records:',len(suspicious))"]},
